          ],
          "params": [],
          "returnType": null,
          "description": "true on the frame the AGGREGATE value — the strongest of every bound source — crossed above the action's own threshold. Bound sources are replayed in the true order their channels changed, so a value that crosses the threshold twice within one frame (0.4 → 0.7 → 0.4 at threshold 0.5) sets both pressed and released on that same frame, while a source that never actually reaches the threshold (0 → 0.1 → 0 at threshold 0.5) sets neither. A second, alternative source tapping while a first stays continuously active never manufactures an edge either, because the aggregate itself never drops below threshold."
        },
        {
          "name": "released",
          "signature": "released: boolean",
          "signatureTokens": [
            {
              "text": "released",
              "kind": "name"
            },
            {
